# Line-ending policy.
#
# Context: this repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so every text blob
# committed so far (including all the .py files) carries CRLF. That is harmless for Python, JSON
# and YAML — every parser on every platform accepts CRLF — so those files are deliberately left
# alone rather than renormalized, which would rewrite the entire repository in one noisy commit
# for no behavioural gain.
#
# Shell scripts are the exception, and the reason this file exists at all. They are executed by
# Linux build images (Render's Python runtime, Vercel's build container), where a CRLF script
# fails hard and confusingly: `set -euo pipefail\r` is an invalid option and a `#!/usr/bin/env
# bash\r` shebang resolves to an interpreter named `bash\r`. Neither error mentions line endings.
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf in both directions, so these files are LF in the index and LF
# in every working tree, on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
